                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I bought this at the end of the last decade and just finished it yesterday. It was better than I expected it to be and somehow better than what I'm used to with FPS games.\n\nTo say what Penguins Arena is exactly it's an FPS game with SSB features. Anywhere from 2-4 teams or penguins all waddle to and fro hurling their snowballs at each other or give a smack. There's also a handful of items/weapons you can acquire, including bear claws to get more traction, a shield to reduce knockback (Sometimes), a bag of fish to smack penguins, a fish bomb that knocks back friend, foe and yourself alike and a mine that sends penguins flying faster than a golf ball.\n\nTo get through the bad first is that there are a handful of official maps that aren't the best. The one that's just a wide expanse with one hill is quite notorious for having long matches. Also the AI for the penguins is a tad bonkers. But that is what really makes the game as fun as it can be in my opinion.\n\nThey will not hesitate to give you hell in a handbasket for a challenge and when you're the last one left they'll hunt you down until someone dies. As for my gripe they do tend to be a pain to actually knockout sometimes and even refuse to let you win.\n\nOf course, all that said I prefer this to actual FPS games like CS or even TF2 which I have a love/hate relationship with. My reasoning being that this game has a better gameplay loop than those. When you die in any other FPS game it's a stab at your soul, every loss a tarnish to your pride. Losing is a part of the gameplay experience, makes you learn and sometimes losing can be more fun than winning.\n\nBut my problem is me. When I used to play against people/bots I always thought they were on par with me and didn't want to stomp me out. But that is not what FPS games are now, when you get in a match you are always up against a handful of people who are better than you are at playing while always being at a disadvantage (Bad teams, people leaving, not getting a chance to shoot etc.).\n\nThat problem isn't in this game. It's gameplay loop is short enough not to leave you out of the fight, you can pick and choose your fights and even on the hardest difficulty you won't be left in the dust because someone is better than you. It can be a bit samey by the time you've played however many matches but luckily there are achievements and they only took me a little over 7 hours and the custom map 'Only one king' to get them all.\n\n8/10 Great game, maybe you might also get to play the multiplayer. I didn't but it's there nyano desu.",
